    "rawMarkdown": "## Before the First Page\n\nThis is a story about two people, one small word, and a great deal of silence that slowly learned how to talk.\n\nMost of this story happened. The dates, messages, calls, promises and milestones are drawn from Waqas and Shajer’s real relationship. The telling has been shaped: scenes are arranged, transitions tightened, and descriptions sometimes give a memory its atmosphere. That shaping should never be mistaken for a new event. Messages reproduced from the source are kept as written. Where Waqas imagines what Shajer might have thought, it is only his guess, and she is welcome to correct it. The final part looks ahead to the wedding and the life after it. It is hopeful fiction, written with love rather than prophecy.\n\nIf this story has a soundtrack, it begins with a piano playing in another room. It carries the warmth of a Korean romance drama, the humour of two people learning each other, and the faith of two hearts that keep saying Alhamdulillah.\n\nRead it with something warm to drink. And when you reach the umbrella scene, remember that the future pages are wishes, not memories.\n"
