    "imageKey": null,
    "rawMarkdown": "## Episode 5 · The Promise\n\n*Monday, 7 September, and Wednesday, 9 September · Now playing: a single violin, and then the sound of a held breath*\n\nIt was not an anniversary. It was not a festival, or a birthday, or any date that anyone would have thought to circle. It was a Monday, and at five in the afternoon a message arrived that was long enough for Waqas to know, before he read a word, that it had been written carefully.\n\nHe read it standing up. Then sitting down. Then, for no reason he could explain, standing up again.\n\n> I promise to stay with you till the very end of my life.\n> No matter the circumstances, every up and every down, we’ll face it together.\n> I will never leave you alone in anything.\n> We’ll be each other’s better half, and build a life that’s loving, peaceful, and full of respect. 💞\n\nSome sentences change the temperature of a room. This was one.\n\nHe had spent days wondering, in the unspoken way of a careful man, whether she felt even a fraction of what he felt. Now it was there in her own words: not a hint, not a joke wrapped around a feeling, but a promise.\n\nShe had said it first. He would remember that for the rest of his life.\n\nHe did not answer at once. He wanted to get it right. He wrote an answer and deleted it. He wrote another and deleted that too. Dinner came and went. The house grew quiet.\n\nAnd then, at midnight, as the date turned over from the seventh to the eighth, he sent his own.\n\n> Shajer,\n> I promise to try my best, every single day, to make you happy.\n> I pray we stay together till the end, through every high and every low.\n> Let’s tackle it all as one team.\n> I could never picture anyone else beside me.\n> You hold the most special place in my heart.\n\nHe chose midnight on purpose. A promise, he felt, should be the first thing of a new day, not the last thing of an old one.\n\nIf anyone had asked him later when it began, he might have given the date of the engagement, or the first message. But the seventh of September would always matter. That was the day two people who had barely spoken made, in plain words, the biggest promise of their lives, and meant it.\n\nTheir first real vow, he would call it. Before the first call. Before the first laugh. Before either had heard the other speak at length.\n\n*Wednesday, 9 September · 8:03 PM*\n\nTwo days later, Waqas sent Shajer a link to the small world he had begun building for her: For Shajer. She received it at 8:03 in the evening.\n\nHer reply was brief:\n\n> mashallah🤌🏻.\n\nHe kept that moment beside the promise. The app would grow over time, but the first gift was the link itself, and the fact that she had opened the door he had made.\n"
