    "rawMarkdown": "## Episode 7 · Without Any Expectation\n\n*Monday, 21 September, to Thursday, 24 September · Now playing: a violin, one long note, held*\n\nOn the twenty-first, Shajer told him she missed him.\n\nShe told him she missed him.\n\nHe read the message more than once. It became one of those sentences he kept returning to, alongside the promise and the voice note, a small thing that had found a permanent place in his memory.\n\nTwo days later, at 3:07 on Wednesday afternoon, the twenty-third of September, Waqas did something that took courage.\n\nHe typed it.\n\n> I LOVE YOU.. no matter what.. fovervee and ever and ever till infinity.. without any expectation till the last minute.. Inshallah.. that will be my dua..\n\nHe noticed the typo the next day. Fovervee. He decided not to apologise for it. It was, he felt, an honest word: forever typed too quickly by someone who meant it.\n\nHe had written without any expectation, and he meant it. That turned out to be the difficult part. He did not ask her to answer. He told himself he was not waiting by the phone.\n\nThat was not entirely true. He waited.\n\nThe next afternoon, at half past four, he did something braver than the confession. He sent his first voice note.\n\nIt was two words long: Assalamu alaikum.\n\nHe recorded the greeting more than once. The first attempts did not sound quite right to him. Eventually he sent the version he could live with, because a voice did not have to be perfect to be true.\n\nFour days passed, counting from the confession. He did not ask for an answer.\n\nLoving someone without expectation was a discipline. At first it felt like standing still in the rain. Then, slowly, it began to feel like trust and prayer.\n"
