    "imageKey": "cover",
    "imageCaption": "Yours, from the first Salaam and every morning after — Waqas.",
    "rawMarkdown": "# A Letter to Shajer\n\n*11 November 2026*\n\nMy Ruhi,\n\nIf you are reading this, you have reached the end of the story I wanted to give you. It is not the end of our story. It is only where these pages stop.\n\nI am not always good at saying large things aloud. You know that. You have heard my voice hesitate on Assalamu alaikum, and you have never made me feel foolish for it. So I did what I often do when my voice runs out. I wrote.\n\nI wrote down the photograph in light green, the first Salaam, the day I chose you, your promise and mine, the calls for Fajr, the messages, the distance, and the morning when a familiar greeting became an ordinary sentence spoken in your voice. I wrote the moments I could remember and tried not to pretend I knew the ones I could not.\n\nThen I wrote a future. The umbrella, the wedding, the quiet after the guests, the first Tuesday. Those pages are not memories. They are hopes. I wrote them because I want a life in which we keep finding one another in ordinary days, not only in the beautiful ones.\n\nI do not know every detail of what is to come. I hope there will be rain, tea, laughter, and arguments we learn to settle before sleep. I hope we keep asking each other whether we have eaten. I hope we keep making room for the truth, even when it is difficult to say.\n\nI know one thing. If life gave me a thousand more times to live it, I would choose you. I said it once. I will go on saying it.\n\nFifty days, Ruhi. I am counting. And I hope the days after them will give us more stories than these pages can hold.\n\nYours, from the first Salaam and every morning after,\nWaqas\n\n*P.S. Khana khaya?*\n\n> Still Writing."
